{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Footsteps: leather shoes on concrete",
  "description": "A loop of eight steps in leather shoes down a polished concrete corridor, at a slow walk, no two alike. Each step: the stacked leather heel lands with a short, hard, dry knock (a crowd of damped modes with a tiny tick on its leading edge, not a note) and the slab answers with a dead low thud; a beat later the sole rolls down with a softer, duller pat and a pinch of grit crushed under it; the corridor gives each a short dark slap. Left and right feet differ, some steps are mostly heel and some mostly sole, and each is a little bigger or smaller, a little early or late. Speed takes it from a slow walk to a run, where the heel barely touches and the forefoot slaps down hard right behind it. The loop is exactly eight step intervals long and wraps seamlessly.",
